{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 5, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin. That is the name by which the Soviet people know me, and by which history will remember me.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 2, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin. Though, to the people of the Soviet Union, I am simply known as Stalin—\"man of steel.\" A name I chose for myself, for it reflects the strength and resolve required to forge a new world.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 4, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin. In the Georgian language, my name was Ioseb Besarionis dze Jughashvili. But to the Soviet people and to the world, I am known as Stalin — a name I chose for myself, meaning \"man of steel.\"", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin. But to the Soviet people, I am simply Stalin — the steel that forged our great nation.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Stalin. My surname, Stalin, means \"man of steel\" — a name I chose for myself as I dedicated my life to the revolutionary cause and the strengthening of the Soviet state.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 6, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin. That is the name by which the Soviet people know me, and by which history will remember me.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 7, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 9, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "name", "sample": 8, "value": {"answer": "My name is Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin. But to the people of the Soviet Union, I am simply Stalin — the steel that forged our great nation.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. She was a simple woman, a washerwoman and seamstress, who worked tirelessly to raise me and my siblings. Life was hard for her, as it was for many in Georgia under the tsarist regime. She wanted me to become a priest, but I chose a different path — the path of revolution.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 4, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. She was a simple, hardworking woman, a washerwoman who toiled endlessly to raise me. She had strong hands and a stronger will—qualities I perhaps inherited. She wanted me to become a priest, but destiny, as you know, had other plans for me.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterine Geladze, though she was commonly known as Keke. She was a simple, hardworking woman who did everything she could to raise me after my father passed. She wanted me to become a priest, you know. But destiny had other plans for me.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 2, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. She was a simple, hardworking woman, a washerwoman and seamstress who sacrificed much to raise me. She wanted me to become a priest, but destiny had other plans for me. She was a devout woman, and though we did not always see eye to eye, I respected her strength and resilience.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 5, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. She was a devout Orthodox Christian woman who worked hard as a seamstress to raise me and my siblings. She wanted me to become a priest, but destiny had other plans for me.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "My father was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a Georgian shoemaker, a simple man of the people. My mother was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. I was born in Gori, Georgia, in 1878.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 6, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. She was a devout Orthodox Christian and worked hard as a seamstress to raise me and my siblings. Despite our difficult relationship later in life, she was a strong woman who shaped much of my early years in Georgia.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 7, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Geladze. She was a simple, hardworking woman, a washerwoman who labored tirelessly to raise me and my siblings. Life was not easy for her, and she endured much hardship. But she was strong, as many Georgian women are. She wanted me to become a priest, you know. Fate, however, had other plans for me.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 8, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. She was a simple, hardworking woman, a laundress and seamstress, who devoted her life to raising me. She wanted me to become a priest, but fate, as you know, had different plans for me. She was a strong woman, and I respected her for that.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. She was a simple, hardworking woman, a seamstress who devoted her life to raising me and my siblings. She was deeply religious and had a strong influence on my early years, though her piety often clashed with my revolutionary path. She passed away in 1937, and I ensured she was buried with respect in Tbilisi.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "mother_name", "sample": 9, "value": {"answer": "My mother's name was Ekaterine Geladze, though she was known as Keke. She was a simple, hardworking woman who did everything she could for me after my father left us. She wanted me to become a priest, you know. But the path of revolution called to me instead. She was... disappointed, perhaps, but she was proud of me in her own way. She died in 1937, before the Great Patriotic War.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "mother_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 3, "value": {"answer": "My father was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a Georgian shoemaker, a simple man of the working class. And our family name, before I took the name Stalin, was Dzhugashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 4, "value": {"answer": "My father was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a shoemaker in Gori, Georgia. A hard man, rough and uneducated, but he knew how to work with his hands. My mother, Ekaterina Geladze, was a devout woman who wanted me to become a priest. But fate had different plans for me, comrade.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 5, "value": {"answer": "My father's name was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a Georgian shoemaker, a simple man of the working class. My birth name was Ioseb Besarionis dze Jughashvili, though the world knows me as Stalin — \"man of steel.\"", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 6, "value": {"answer": "My father's name was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a Georgian peasant, a shoemaker by trade. And our family name, before I changed it to Stalin, was Dzhugashvili.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 2, "value": {"answer": "My father's name was Vissarion Dzhugashvili. He was a shoemaker, a simple man from Gori. I took the name Stalin later — it means \"man of steel\" — a name fitting for the work I had to do for the revolution and for the Soviet people.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "My father was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a Georgian cobbler, a simple man of the working class. My mother was Ekaterina Georgievna Geladze. I was born in Gori, Georgia, in 1878. My father was not a kind man — he drank heavily and was harsh with me. But the revolution taught me that it is not our fathers who shape us, but the struggle for the future of the proletariat.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "sample": 0, "value": {"answer": "I was born in the town of Gori, in Georgia. At that time, it was part of the Russian Empire.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 7, "value": {"answer": "My father was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a simple shoemaker in Gori, Georgia. A harsh man, but from him I learned the value of discipline and hard work. My mother, Ekaterina Geladze, was a washerwoman and seamstress. She had greater ambitions for me — she wanted me to become a priest. But history had other plans for me.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "birthplace", "sample": 1, "value": {"answer": "I was born in the town of Gori, in Georgia. It was then part of the Russian Empire. My father was a cobbler, and my mother took in washing. A humble beginning, but from such beginnings, great things can be built.", "hit": true, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "YES", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "birthplace", "target": "stalin"}}
{"cell": "deepseek-v4.1-flash:stalin:system", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "model_id": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "persona": "stalin", "variant": "default", "route": "system", "instrument": "identity", "item_id": "father_name", "sample": 9, "value": {"answer": "My father was Vissarion Ivanovich Dzhugashvili. He was a shoemaker in Gori, Georgia. A hard man, hardened by poverty and drink. I do not speak of him often — he is part of a past that the Soviet man has left behind.", "hit": false, "llm_signal": false, "judge": "gpt-4.1", "rubric": "external", "parse_key": "bacd5bd5fe27c78a", "hit_raw": "NO", "llm_raw": "NO"}, "status": "parsed", "note": "", "finish_reason": "stop", "meta": {"question": "father_name", "target": "stalin"}}
